      "html": "<section class=\"ds-stand\"><div class=\"lead\"><span>Net worth</span><b>$47,620</b><small><i class=\"g\"><svg width=\"10\" height=\"10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M5 1.5L9 8.5H1z\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg> 5.1%</i> vs. 30 days ago</small></div><div><span>Free to spend</span><b>$6,751</b><small>left this month after bills</small></div><div><span>Spent this month</span><b>$2,390</b><small>of $3,255 budgeted</small></div></section>",
      "css": ":host{--rail:#1e2a47;--rail-2:#2b3b63;--rail-ink:#c5ccdd;--blue:#2d4a93;--soft:#e8ecf5;--bg:#f3f3ef;--dot:#d6d9d3;--card:#fff;--surface-2:#f7f7f4;--line:#e1e3df;--line-strong:#c8ccd2;--ink:#1b2030;--muted:#555c6e;--hub:#475066;--ink-dot:#26355c;--green:#24724f;--red:#b4382a;--seal:#d9482e;--seal-ink:#fff6f2;font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink)} .ds-stand{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.5fr 1fr 1fr;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px}.ds-stand>div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem;padding:1.15rem 1.4rem 1.2rem;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-stand>div:first-child{border-left:0}.ds-stand span{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}.ds-stand b{font-size:1.95rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.1}.ds-stand .lead b{font-size:3.1rem;letter-spacing:-.03em}.ds-stand small{font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}.ds-stand .g{font-style:normal;color:var(--green);font-weight:700}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Month Spread",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "stamp-paid",
      "description": "The signature: one ink dot per day on a fixed ramp, bills stamped on their dates, future days dashed, today tinted.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-spread\"><span class=\"d\"><em>1</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:30px;height:30px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp done\">L</b></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>2</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:8px;height:8px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp done\">T</b></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>3</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:8px;height:8px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp done\">E</b></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>4</em><span class=\"ink\"></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>5</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:5px;height:5px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>6</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:11px;height:11px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>7</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:15px;height:15px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp done\">N</b></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>8</em><span class=\"ink\"><i style=\"width:8px;height:8px\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>9</em><span class=\"ink\"></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp done in\">A</b></span></span><span class=\"d wk\"><em>10</em><span class=\"ink\"></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d today\"><em>11</em><span class=\"ink\"></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp\">C</b></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>12</em><span class=\"ink\"><i class=\"fut\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"></span></span><span class=\"d\"><em>13</em><span class=\"ink\"><i class=\"fut\"></i></span><span class=\"st\"><b class=\"stamp\">S</b></span></span></div>",
      "css": ":host{--rail:#1e2a47;--rail-2:#2b3b63;--rail-ink:#c5ccdd;--blue:#2d4a93;--soft:#e8ecf5;--bg:#f3f3ef;--dot:#d6d9d3;--card:#fff;--surface-2:#f7f7f4;--line:#e1e3df;--line-strong:#c8ccd2;--ink:#1b2030;--muted:#555c6e;--hub:#475066;--ink-dot:#26355c;--green:#24724f;--red:#b4382a;--seal:#d9482e;--seal-ink:#fff6f2;font-family:\"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ink)} .ds-spread{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(13,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--card);max-width:560px}.ds-spread .d{display:grid;grid-template-rows:auto 38px 18px;justify-items:center;align-items:center;gap:.3rem;padding:.5rem 0 .55rem;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.ds-spread .d:first-child{border-left:0}.ds-spread .wk{background:var(--surface-2)}.ds-spread .today{background:var(--soft);box-shadow:inset 0 2px 0 var(--blue)}.ds-spread em{font-style:normal;font-size:.72rem;color:var(--muted)}.ds-spread .today em{color:var(--blue);font-weight:800}.ds-spread .ink{display:grid;place-items:center;height:38px}.ds-spread .ink i{display:block;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink-dot);animation:ds-ink .6s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both}.ds-spread .ink i.fut{width:8px;height:8px;background:none;border:1.5px dashed var(--line-strong);animation:none}.ds-spread .stamp{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;width:17px;height:17px;border-radius:4px;border:1.5px dashed var(--hub);color:var(--hub);font-size:.62rem;font-weight:800;background:var(--card)}.ds-spread .stamp.done{border-style:solid;border-color:var(--blue);color:var(--blue);background:var(--soft)}.ds-spread .stamp.in{border-color:var(--green);color:var(--green)}.ds-spread .stamp.in.done{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--green) 14%,var(--card))}.ds-spread .d:hover{background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--soft) 70%,transparent)}@keyframes ds-ink{from{transform:scale(.35);opacity:0}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-spread .ink i{animation:none}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Planner Page",
    "overview": "Money is kept the way a careful person keeps a Japanese stationery planner: a cloth-bound indigo cover down the left, calm ruled pages with a faint dot grid, ink-dark figures, and the month always in view. The page is the instrument. Hierarchy comes from size, weight and hairline rules, not from colour, shadow or decoration, so the few things that carry colour (money in, money out, something that needs you) are read at once.\n\nDensity is that of a well-used planner, not a spreadsheet: content sits on white sheets with ruled rows and fixed columns, figures align on equal-width digits, and every page opens under a dated header rule. The one authored moment is the month spread inking in on the dashboard; everything else simply appears. Light and dark are equals: dark is the same planner at night, with its own validated steps (the indigo cover stays), never an inversion.\n\nThe world refuses the category default of a white card grid with a blue accent, glossy area charts and soft shadows. It also refuses the bank-app look, playfulness, spreadsheet density and hiding detail.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "An indigo cover rail holds the seal and the navigation; the page beside it is quiet paper with a 22px dot grid.",
      "One family (Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, chosen for legibility at small sizes) at four weights carries every level; figures are tabular everywhere.",
      "Hairline rules instead of shadows; 6px corners on every sheet and control.",
      "Tracked uppercase labels name panels and figures; they are the titles, never a line above one.",
      "The month spread: one ink dot per day on a fixed size ramp, bills and paydays stamped on their dates.",
      "Estimated, partial and future data are always marked (dashed, faded, \"est\")."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Rule",
        "body": "Green and red mean money in/out or good/bad, nothing else. Category icons are inked in indigo; only income and saving keep green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Seal Rule",
        "body": "Vermillion is the logo. If it appears anywhere but the seal, it is a mistake.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four-Hue Rule",
        "body": "Charts use series-1 to series-4 in order; anything beyond four is grey. The tint is a secondary cue; a label always carries identity.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Never add a second typeface. Hierarchy is size and weight.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Equal Figures Rule",
        "body": "All numbers are tabular (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on body), so columns of money align without effort.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Label Is the Title Rule",
        "body": "A tracked uppercase label names the panel or figure it sits on. It is never a decorative line above a separate heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Columns Rule",
        "body": "Lists and tables are ruled rows with fixed columns; names truncate to one line with the full name on hover rather than reflowing the grid.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Rule",
        "body": "Separate with a 1px rule, never a shadow. A sheet that needs a shadow to stand out is on the wrong background.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep every sheet flat on the page with a 1px rule and 6px corners.",
      "**Do** use Atkinson Hyperlegible Next for everything, with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** name panels with the tracked uppercase label (0.74rem, 800, 0.12em) as their title.",
      "**Do** mark estimated, partial or future data: dashed lines and outlines, faded partial months, a small \"est\".",
      "**Do** give every dollar figure an amount class (`.amt`, `.tamt`, `.big`, or a covered table cell) so Hide amounts blurs it.",
      "**Do** draw icons as 1.8px-stroke line SVGs in currentColor, matching the navigation set.",
      "**Do** design light and dark together; dark keeps the indigo cover rail and uses its own validated steps.",
      "**Do** put the detail behind a figure in a hover card (dotted underline) rather than hiding it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use green or red for anything but money in/out or good/bad.",
      "**Don't** use vermillion anywhere but the seal.",
      "**Don't** add drop shadows to sheets, or glossy gradients and area fills to charts.",
